extension BundledDomainSkills {
    static let officialDefinitions: [Definition] = [
        Definition(id: "floe-pdf", name: "PDF Workbench", description: "Native PDF editing, region reflow, images, forms, annotations, OCR and verified raster redaction.", version: "1.2.0", exposed: true, markdown: "## PDF workbench\nFollow this closed loop for PDF tasks:\n1. **Inspect first**: `document.pdf.inspect` for page count, metadata, text, and query matches before planning any edit.\n2. **Render only relevant pages** with `document.pdf.render` (single page or a spec like \"1-3,5\") when visual evidence is needed.\n3. **Compose**: `document.pdf.merge` (2-10 PDFs in order), `document.pdf.split` (extract pages \"1-3,5,8-10\"), `document.pdf.fromImages` (one image per page).\n4. **Edit** with `document.pdf.edit`: page removal, rotations, watermarks and page numbers. `replaceText` performs exact case-sensitive native content-stream edits, never a white cover. Existing-font replacements must fit the original bounds. For multi-object text or longer paragraphs, use `operations` action `replaceRegion`: inspect the native object inventory, pass the exact `expectedObjectCount` and enclosing `bounds`, and supply new text/fontSize. CoreText reflows and embeds searchable Unicode text; overflowing text, partial object intersections and mixed nested forms fail without saving. `addText` inserts a new text region. This is ordinary editing, not secure redaction.\n5. **Advanced operations** require `expectedSHA256` from the same inspection. Coordinates are unrotated PDF points with a lower-left origin. Page operations include reorderPages (every page exactly once), cropPage (visual crop only, NOT deletion), insertBlankPage. Annotation operations add/update/remove note, freeText, markup, shapes, ink and lines; use 0-based annotationIndex from the current revision. Images support insertImage/replaceImage/removeImage with workspace imagePath, explicit bounds and expected object count for removal. Images stretch to the rectangle; keep its aspect ratio when distortion is unwanted.\n6. **Forms and document structure**: operations createField/setField/removeField support text, checkbox and choice fields. The existing `document.pdf.fillForm` provides additional AcroForm filling including radio/option lists. setMetadata updates title/author/subject/creator/keywords (empty value removes that attribute). setBookmarks replaces the top-level bookmark list. `flattenAnnotations` requires acceptFlattening after consent, preserves page content but removes interactivity; it is NOT secure redaction.\n7. **OCR and redaction**: searchableOCR uses on-device Vision and rebuilds pages with a recognized, searchable text layer; text may contain recognition errors. rasterRedact rebuilds ALL pages from fresh raster images, masking selected regions before encoding. It copies no original text streams, annotations, forms, attachments, bookmarks or signatures, and verifies image-only output. Both must be the only edit operation and require the user's explicit acceptance of rasterization (acceptRasterization=true). Current bounded workflow accepts up to 50 unrotated pages with matching media/crop boxes. Do not describe ordinary covering, cropping, password protection or flattening as secure deletion. Do not claim PKI signature validation or vector-preserving secure redaction.\n8. **Credentials**: output protection accepts only saved userPasswordRef/ownerPasswordRef references resolved inside the approved executor. `document.pdf.unlock` creates a new decrypted copy using passwordRef and verifies reopening; it requires the correct credential and PDF modification permissions, and rejects signed files. Never put plaintext passwords into tool arguments. Signed files are rejected for ordinary edits; only explicitly accepted rasterized unsigned copies are supported.\n9. **Save to a new output**, reopen with document.pdf.inspect and render changed pages. Existing outputs are refused, including alternate spellings that resolve to the source. Report actual output, digest/reopen evidence and remaining limits. Never silently substitute rasterization or a different editing operation after failure.\n10. **Export**: use document.pdf.export for real searchable text (`text` or page-structured `json`), not Word-layout conversion. Use document.pdf.render for `png` or `jpeg` page images. Empty text from scans requires the separate consented OCR workflow, never invented text.\n"),
        Definition(id: "floe-office", name: "Office Documents", description: "Word, workbook and Markdown creation/inspection/editing with the right tool for each job.", version: "1.1.0", exposed: true, markdown: "## Office document workflow\n- **Word (.docx)**: `document.createWord` generates a real OOXML document; `document.office.inspect` returns stable field IDs; `document.office.updateText` edits those fields (use only explicit IDs from inspect; never guess).\n- **Workbook (.xlsx)**: `document.createWorkbook` builds a spreadsheet from sheet JSON. To **read** cell values quickly use `document.readSheet` (read-only TSV). To **edit** use `document.office.inspect` first — it returns the editable field/formula IDs that `document.office.updateText` consumes. Do not treat readSheet output as editable IDs.\n- **Markdown**: `document.createMarkdown` writes .md/.markdown/.txt only (for .docx use createWord).\n- **Fonts**: before `font.remove`, call `font.list` and reuse the exact digest id — never derive it from a filename.\n- Always reopen/inspect the saved artifact to verify, and save to a new file unless overwrite was explicitly requested."),
        Definition(id: "floe-network", name: "Network Diagnostics", description: "Ping, traceroute, DNS, LAN scan and raw HTTP with the right boundary versus web.fetch.", version: "1.1.0", exposed: true, markdown: "## Network diagnostics workflow\n- `network.ping`, `network.traceroute`, `network.dnsLookup` diagnose reachability on the **local device** by default; pass a paired `hostID` only when the user wants the probe run from that remote host.\n- `network.scanLAN` enumerates the local network — run it only when the user asked for discovery or a LAN diagnostic.\n- `network.http` issues raw HTTP with method/headers/body control subject to network policy. When the goal is **reading a web page as content**, use `web.fetch` instead (returns readable markdown). Use `network.download` to save an authorized URL to a workspace file.\n- Credential URLs and cloud metadata endpoints are blocked; never try to bypass those blocks or exfiltrate instance metadata.")
